================================================================================
3. Derived and patched third-party sources in this repository
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 websocket 2.17 (lwt wrapper)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

src/external/ws_lwt/ws_lwt.ml is a client-only replacement derived from the lwt
wrapper of the websocket library, version 2.17. The wire framing is delegated to
Websocket.Make in vendor/websocket, an in-tree RFC 6455 implementation, so the
format is unchanged.

Source:  https://github.com/vbmithr/ocaml-websocket
License: ISC

Copyright (c) Vincent Bernardoff and contributors

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.2 Vendored OCaml sources
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The OxCaml-compatible copies of lwt, ssl, lwt_ssl, base64, mtime, yojson,
msgpck, notty-community, uutf, ctypes and integers now live under vendor/ and
are built by this repository. Exact versions, licenses and applied patches are
listed in vendor/README.md. The remaining vendor libraries (digestif, uri,
ipaddr, conduit-lwt-unix, cohttp, cohttp-lwt, cohttp-lwt-unix, websocket,
alcotest and mirage-crypto-rng) are original implementations written for dio
and are covered by this repository's LICENSE.

================================================================================
4. In-tree OCaml libraries
================================================================================

These libraries are built from source in this repository (vendor/) and
statically linked into dio, dio-dashboard and dio-oracle. The only OCaml
library linked from opam is secp256k1; its build-time-only dependencies
(base, stdio, dune-configurator) are not linked. The compiler runtime is the
external toolchain component.

Component             Location              License                    Upstream
--------------------- --------------------- -------------------------- --------------------------
lwt, lwt.unix         vendor/lwt            MIT                        ocaml-lwt 6.0.0+ox
ssl                   vendor/ssl            LGPL-2.1 + OpenSSL exc.    ocaml-ssl 0.7.0
lwt_ssl               vendor/lwt_ssl        LGPL-2.1 + OpenSSL exc.    lwt_ssl 1.2.0
base64                vendor/base64         ISC                        base64 3.5.2
mtime                 vendor/mtime          ISC                        mtime 2.2.0
yojson                vendor/yojson         BSD-3-Clause               yojson 2.2.2+ox
msgpck                vendor/msgpck         ISC                        msgpck 1.7
notty-community       vendor/notty          ISC                        notty 0.2.4
uutf                  vendor/uutf           ISC                        uutf 1.0.4+ox
ctypes                vendor/ctypes         MIT                        ctypes 0.24.0+ox
integers              vendor/integers       MIT                        integers 0.8.0
secp256k1             opam                  MIT                        secp256k1 0.5.0

The following vendor directories are original implementations written for dio
and are covered by this repository's LICENSE: digestif, uri, ipaddr,
conduit-lwt-unix, cohttp, cohttp-lwt, cohttp-lwt-unix, websocket, alcotest and
mirage-crypto-rng.

Build-, test-, and documentation-only dependencies that are not shipped:
dune (MIT), dune-configurator (MIT), odoc (ISC).

Full texts: MIT, ISC, BSD-2-Clause and BSD-3-Clause are in section 6. The
LGPL-2.1 + OpenSSL exemption texts are in vendor/ssl/COPYING and
vendor/lwt_ssl/COPYING. Per-library license files are also kept alongside each
vendored source tree.


================================================================================
5. Container base OS and runtime system libraries
================================================================================

Base image: Ubuntu 22.04 LTS (pinned by digest in Dockerfile).

Runtime packages installed into the image: libffi8, libgmp10, libpcre3,
libssl3, libpq5, zlib1g, libjemalloc2, ca-certificates, netbase.

These are unmodified Ubuntu packages. Each package's copyright and license text
is installed by the distribution at /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside
the image. Principal licenses:

  libffi8          MIT
  libgmp10         LGPL-3.0-or-later or GPL-2.0-or-later
  libpcre3         BSD-3-Clause
  libssl3          Apache-2.0
  libpq5           PostgreSQL
  zlib1g           Zlib
  libjemalloc2     BSD-2-Clause
  ca-certificates  MPL-2.0
  netbase          GPL-2.0


